    {
      "id": "llnU9lJnUPbYM12IndlIA",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -621.3935398961765,
      "y": 1035.3784625119386,
      "width": 1840.466552734375,
      "height": 525,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "as",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1035583763,
      "version": 169,
      "versionNonce": 905848130,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793539231223,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Open Questions\n1. The app crashes after step 1 but before step 2. This is follow-up 1.\n2. Kafka is slow or down at step 2. Does checkout still respond in 200 ms? What do you return?\n3.  inventory reservation is now asynchronous, so checkout says \"order placed\" before any stock is reserved. \n    What happens if the item is out of stock, and what does the customer see?\n4. Idempotency race at the API. Two identical requests arrive at the same moment, both check, \n    both find nothing, and both create the order. How do you prevent that?\n5. Duplicates in consumers. Committing after processing means at-least-once delivery, \n    so a message can be processed twice. Where do you stop a second confirmation email or double loyalty points (requirement 3)?\n6. Partition count. How many partitions do you need? Adding them later remaps keys and can break \n    per-order ordering, so plan for the most instances your slowest consumer will ever need.\n7. Where a new consumer starts reading. When the fraud check service joins, does it start from the \n    newest messages or from the beginning? How long does Kafka keep messages?\n8. Retries and failures. This comes from the problem; we haven't discussed it yet. The email provider is down for 10 minutes, \n    or one message always fails (follow-up 2). How does the consumer retry without blocking every message behind it in that partition?",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Open Questions\n1. The app crashes after step 1 but before step 2. This is follow-up 1.\n2. Kafka is slow or down at step 2. Does checkout still respond in 200 ms? What do you return?\n3.  inventory reservation is now asynchronous, so checkout says \"order placed\" before any stock is reserved. \n    What happens if the item is out of stock, and what does the customer see?\n4. Idempotency race at the API. Two identical requests arrive at the same moment, both check, \n    both find nothing, and both create the order. How do you prevent that?\n5. Duplicates in consumers. Committing after processing means at-least-once delivery, \n    so a message can be processed twice. Where do you stop a second confirmation email or double loyalty points (requirement 3)?\n6. Partition count. How many partitions do you need? Adding them later remaps keys and can break \n    per-order ordering, so plan for the most instances your slowest consumer will ever need.\n7. Where a new consumer starts reading. When the fraud check service joins, does it start from the \n    newest messages or from the beginning? How long does Kafka keep messages?\n8. Retries and failures. This comes from the problem; we haven't discussed it yet. The email provider is down for 10 minutes, \n    or one message always fails (follow-up 2). How does the consumer retry without blocking every message behind it in that partition?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
